From: local diagnostic patch
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: skip suspend reset for switcheroo-off GPUs

vga_switcheroo manual OFF asks amdgpu to suspend the inactive GPU, then
asks the platform handler to cut its power.  The DRM device remains bound
and its switch_power_state is set to DRM_SWITCH_POWER_OFF.

amdgpu_device_prepare(), amdgpu_device_suspend(), and
amdgpu_device_resume() already avoid hardware access in this state.  Apply
the same rule to the noirq suspend callback.  Otherwise a deep suspend
attempts to reset a physically absent GPU and can abort system suspend.

This is a local test patch for the MacBookPro11,5 investigation.  Add a
proper Signed-off-by line and confirm the Fixes tag with git blame before
upstream submission.

Likely-Fixes: daf8de0874ab5 ("drm/amdgpu: always reset the asic in suspend (v2)")
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
@@ -2639,6 +2639,9 @@ static int amdgpu_pmops_suspend_noirq(struct device *dev)
 	struct amdgpu_device *adev = drm_to_adev(drm_dev);
 	int r;
 
+	if (drm_dev->switch_power_state == DRM_SWITCH_POWER_OFF)
+		return 0;
+
 	if (amdgpu_acpi_should_gpu_reset(adev)) {
 		amdgpu_device_lock_reset_domain(adev->reset_domain);
 		r = amdgpu_asic_reset(adev);
-- 
